  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected: the relative 'which' of 'which a great king of Israel builded' is the object of the verb and realizes the object suffix of בְּנָהִי (rule 18), so it goes to the suffix and the waw, for which the ASV writes no separate connective, is unrepresented (rule 17: a pronoun the relative realizes takes it before the waw does). Contrast EZR.5.12, where 'who' is the subject relative and no pronoun realizes it, so it is the waw's."
  ]
